From: Sage Ross <ragesoss@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:49:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(sfont): hard-left and hard-right zones in the stereo
 players

Checks sfplay, sfplay3 and sflooper with zones panned to -500 and +500,
and with preset and instrument pans that add up past either end. Both
channels must stay finite, the far channel exactly zero and the near one
at the zone's full level. Before #3404, gcc -ffast-math builds with FMA
gave NaN on the right channel at -500 (#3403); this test fails there
without that fix. A tiny embedded SoundFont, as in test_sfplay_envelopes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../commandline/test_sfplay_pan_endpoints.csd | 106 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 106 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/commandline/test_sfplay_pan_endpoints.csd

diff --git a/tests/commandline/test_sfplay_pan_endpoints.csd b/tests/commandline/test_sfplay_pan_endpoints.csd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2864c87
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/commandline/test_sfplay_pan_endpoints.csd
@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
